The native Track B family inverse-generates noncommutative rational sums of hermitian squares based on the [paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2101.02314). All local G1–G9 gates pass. However:

- Medium held bare but was solved 2/3 with the structural hint.
- The permitted move to hard was solved bare 1/3.
- Doubling to the next genuine size requires 328 logical answer atoms, exceeding the 256-atom limit.

No `REJECTED.md` was created, as required for `cap_bound`.
